1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:02,327
August nineteen fifty-five.

2
00:00:02,327 --> 00:00:04,100
A farmhouse in Kentucky.

3
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:08,237
Eleven people inside, and something outside the windows.

4
00:00:08,237 --> 00:00:15,033
For about four hours, the family fired shotguns at small glowing figures that would not die.

5
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:24,147
They described a creature about three feet tall, silvery, with huge ears, enormous eyes, and arms that nearly touched the ground.

6
00:00:24,147 --> 00:00:27,633
They said bullets rang off it like hitting a bucket.

7
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:28,963
Police came.

8
00:00:28,963 --> 00:00:29,970
Soldiers came.

9
00:00:29,970 --> 00:00:34,214
They found bullet holes, a terrified family, and no bodies.

10
00:00:34,214 --> 00:00:37,666
And the family never made a cent from the story.

11
00:00:38,133 --> 00:00:40,396
So tonight we keep a night watch.

12
00:00:40,396 --> 00:00:47,733
Hour by hour, we log every claim, sort the evidence from the theory, and ask what really happened at Kelly.

13
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:51,248
Little men from space, or owls in the dark?

14
00:00:51,248 --> 00:00:52,666
Let's begin the log.

15
00:00:57,133 --> 00:00:58,208
Log entry one.

16
00:00:58,208 --> 00:00:58,977
The place.

17
00:00:58,977 --> 00:01:07,966
Kelly is a tiny farming community in Christian County, Kentucky, about seven miles north of the town of Hopkinsville.

18
00:01:08,433 --> 00:01:13,575
The Sutton farmhouse was a rented, run-down home with no running water.

19
00:01:13,575 --> 00:01:18,500
It stood at the end of a dirt road, surrounded by woods and a gully.

20
00:01:18,966 --> 00:01:24,612
Inside lived Glennie Lankford, her sons, and her children, with guests visiting.

21
00:01:24,612 --> 00:01:27,788
Elmer, called Lucky, Sutton rented the house.

22
00:01:27,788 --> 00:01:30,400
Eleven people were there that Sunday.

23
00:01:30,866 --> 00:01:34,042
These were poor, hard-working country people.

24
00:01:34,042 --> 00:01:39,265
They kept guns, as most rural families did, for hunting and for the foxes.

25
00:01:39,265 --> 00:01:41,099
That detail matters later.

26
00:01:41,566 --> 00:01:43,170
The layout matters too.

27
00:01:43,170 --> 00:01:44,495
A well at the back.

28
00:01:44,495 --> 00:01:46,239
A gully beyond the fence.

29
00:01:46,239 --> 00:01:47,355
A few big trees.

30
00:01:47,355 --> 00:01:50,633
And nothing but dark fields in every direction.

31
00:01:51,099 --> 00:01:57,367
That evening, around seven, a visitor named Billy Ray Taylor went out to the well for water.

32
00:01:57,367 --> 00:02:02,000
He came running back, saying he had seen a bright object in the sky.

33
00:02:02,466 --> 00:02:09,375
Taylor said it was bright, with a rainbow-coloured exhaust, and that it landed in the gully beyond the fence.

34
00:02:09,375 --> 00:02:10,642
Nobody believed him.

35
00:02:10,642 --> 00:02:11,466
They laughed.

36
00:02:11,933 --> 00:02:16,906
Then the dogs began barking, then hid under the house and would not come out.

37
00:02:16,906 --> 00:02:18,262
Dogs are good alarms.

38
00:02:18,262 --> 00:02:20,199
Something had frightened them.

39
00:02:20,666 --> 00:02:22,347
Log, seven forty-five.

40
00:02:22,347 --> 00:02:26,854
A glow appears in the yard, coming slowly toward the house.

41
00:02:26,854 --> 00:02:29,833
Taylor and Lucky Sutton go to the door.

42
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:35,470
They said a small glowing figure walked toward them with its hands raised.

43
00:02:35,470 --> 00:02:39,733
Three feet tall, a big head, ears like a bat, a silver shine.

44
00:02:40,199 --> 00:02:42,509
The men did not wait to be polite.

45
00:02:42,509 --> 00:02:44,004
Lucky fired a shotgun.

46
00:02:44,004 --> 00:02:46,177
Taylor fired a twenty-two rifle.

47
00:02:46,177 --> 00:02:49,166
They hit it, they said, and it flipped over.

48
00:02:49,633 --> 00:02:53,662
The creature somersaulted, then scampered off into the dark.

49
00:02:53,662 --> 00:02:56,415
They said it did not fall like an animal.

50
00:02:56,415 --> 00:02:58,966
It floated, almost, and got up unhurt.

51
00:02:59,433 --> 00:03:03,363
The men said the shots rang like hitting a metal bucket.

52
00:03:03,363 --> 00:03:04,907
That is an odd detail.

53
00:03:04,907 --> 00:03:09,399
A shotgun blast against a living thing does not make that sound.

54
00:03:09,866 --> 00:03:12,985
Minutes later, a face appeared at the window.

55
00:03:12,985 --> 00:03:15,203
Taylor fired through the screen.

56
00:03:15,203 --> 00:03:17,907
Another creature climbed onto the roof.

57
00:03:17,907 --> 00:03:20,333
A hand reached down toward a child.

58
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:25,028
On the roof, said the family, a figure crouched in the starlight.

59
00:03:25,028 --> 00:03:28,932
Lucky stepped outside and a clawed hand grabbed at his hair.

60
00:03:28,932 --> 00:03:30,233
He felt it, he said.

61
00:03:30,699 --> 00:03:35,019
Inside, the women gathered the children in the middle of the house.

62
00:03:35,019 --> 00:03:37,405
Glennie Lankford tried to keep order.

63
00:03:37,405 --> 00:03:39,533
Her youngest was seven years old.

64
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:41,619
Hours passed in a loop.

65
00:03:41,619 --> 00:03:42,957
Creatures appeared.

66
00:03:42,957 --> 00:03:43,943
Men shot them.

67
00:03:43,943 --> 00:03:44,929
They vanished.

68
00:03:44,929 --> 00:03:45,985
They came back.

69
00:03:45,985 --> 00:03:50,633
The family had no phone, no neighbours, and no escape but the car.

70
00:03:51,099 --> 00:04:01,233
Around eleven that night, all eleven crammed into two cars and drove to the Hopkinsville police station, seven miles away, ashen and out of breath.

71
00:04:01,699 --> 00:04:06,787
Police chief Greg Russell later said he had never seen people so frightened.

72
00:04:06,787 --> 00:04:09,866
They were not drunk, he noted, and not joking.

73
00:04:10,333 --> 00:04:15,733
Within minutes, more than a dozen officers and soldiers were on the road to the farm.

74
00:04:16,199 --> 00:04:17,533
Log, eleven thirty.

75
00:04:17,533 --> 00:04:25,466
Police from the state, the county, and the city arrive, joined by four military police from nearby Fort Campbell.

76
00:04:25,933 --> 00:04:29,068
They found the evidence the family promised.

77
00:04:29,068 --> 00:04:31,063
Bullet holes in the screens.

78
00:04:31,063 --> 00:04:33,058
Shotgun damage on the walls.

79
00:04:33,058 --> 00:04:35,266
Spent shells all over the yard.

80
00:04:35,733 --> 00:04:38,498
What they did not find was a creature.

81
00:04:38,498 --> 00:04:41,844
No bodies, no blood, no tracks, no spacecraft.

82
00:04:41,844 --> 00:04:43,300
The gully was empty.

83
00:04:43,766 --> 00:04:47,993
One officer noticed a faint glow on the ground near the fence.

84
00:04:47,993 --> 00:04:50,789
It looked, he said, like a strange shine.

85
00:04:50,789 --> 00:04:52,766
He could not say what it was.

86
00:04:53,233 --> 00:04:55,841
Some theories later said it was a meteor.

87
00:04:55,841 --> 00:05:00,866
The Perseid showers and a bright fireball were seen across Kentucky that night.

88
00:05:01,333 --> 00:05:04,670
By two in the morning, the police gave up and left.

89
00:05:04,670 --> 00:05:10,166
Chief Russell said he had seen enough to know the family truly believed their story.

90
00:05:10,633 --> 00:05:13,953
And then, say the Suttons, the creatures came back.

91
00:05:13,953 --> 00:05:18,899
Barely had the cars disappeared before a face looked in at the window again.

92
00:05:19,366 --> 00:05:20,955
The shooting began again.

93
00:05:20,955 --> 00:05:28,266
It went on until about five that morning, when the first grey light arrived and the figures finally stopped coming.

94
00:05:28,733 --> 00:05:30,501
At dawn, the family left.

95
00:05:30,501 --> 00:05:31,987
The farm stood quiet.

96
00:05:31,987 --> 00:05:38,000
The siege, by their count, had lasted about four hours, on and off, across the night.

97
00:05:38,466 --> 00:05:39,281
Log, Monday.

98
00:05:39,281 --> 00:05:40,436
The press arrive.

99
00:05:40,436 --> 00:05:47,566
Reporters from the Kentucky New Era and others filled the town, and the story went national within hours.

100
00:05:48,033 --> 00:05:59,433
Two civilian investigators, Isabel Davis and Ted Bloecher, interviewed the family in nineteen fifty-six and wrote a long report for the Civilian Saucer Intelligence.

101
00:05:59,899 --> 00:06:03,031
They found the accounts remarkably consistent.

102
00:06:03,031 --> 00:06:09,566
The family told the same core story separately, and the details barely changed between tellings.

103
00:06:10,033 --> 00:06:13,156
Sketches were drawn from the descriptions.

104
00:06:13,156 --> 00:06:18,807
A small body, a round head, large pointed ears, long arms, and clawed hands.

105
00:06:18,807 --> 00:06:21,633
Not a classic little green man at all.

106
00:06:22,100 --> 00:06:23,722
Later, the astronomer J.

107
00:06:23,722 --> 00:06:31,633
Allen Hynek, the man who coined the term close encounter, studied the case and thought it deserved serious attention.

108
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:35,410
Notably, the family never sought fame or money.

109
00:06:35,410 --> 00:06:37,804
They had no book deal and no film.

110
00:06:37,804 --> 00:06:40,833
The Suttons mostly wanted to be left alone.

111
00:06:41,300 --> 00:06:42,824
Here is what we have.

112
00:06:42,824 --> 00:06:44,058
A sincere family.

113
00:06:44,058 --> 00:06:45,001
Bullet holes.

114
00:06:45,001 --> 00:06:47,469
Dozens of witnesses to their fear.

115
00:06:47,469 --> 00:06:50,300
And no physical trace of anything else.

116
00:06:50,766 --> 00:06:52,579
Log, the skeptic's file.

117
00:06:52,579 --> 00:06:55,147
A simpler idea: great horned owls.

118
00:06:55,147 --> 00:06:56,355
Check the facts.

119
00:06:56,355 --> 00:07:01,566
They stand about two feet tall, with a wingspan of four or five feet.

120
00:07:02,033 --> 00:07:04,315
They have big round yellow eyes.

121
00:07:04,315 --> 00:07:07,025
Ear tufts that look like pointed ears.

122
00:07:07,025 --> 00:07:07,952
Sharp talons.

123
00:07:07,952 --> 00:07:10,733
And they nest in the woods of Kentucky.

124
00:07:11,199 --> 00:07:15,550
Mother owls defend their nests fiercely and glow faintly in light.

125
00:07:15,550 --> 00:07:19,966
A pair near the farm might have been drawn by the lights and noise.

126
00:07:20,433 --> 00:07:30,466
Skeptoid and investigators like Joe Nickell argue that the family, already scared by the meteor, mistook owls on the roof and in the trees for monsters.

127
00:07:30,933 --> 00:07:33,063
What of bullets that did nothing?

128
00:07:33,063 --> 00:07:40,100
The men fired through screens and darkness, probably missing, and sometimes hitting thick feathers, not bone.

129
00:07:40,566 --> 00:07:46,380
The 'bucket' sound could have been pellets striking the tin roof or metal rim of the well.

130
00:07:46,380 --> 00:07:47,930
And the 'floating' walk?

131
00:07:47,930 --> 00:07:49,933
Shadows, wind, panic and lamps.

132
00:07:50,399 --> 00:07:53,603
Add fear, exhaustion, and a hot August night.

133
00:07:53,603 --> 00:07:59,866
A group under stress can build the same story together, each person confirming the last.

134
00:08:00,333 --> 00:08:02,446
But some details still resist.

135
00:08:02,446 --> 00:08:09,349
The creatures' behaviour, the long hours, and the way adults and children described the same face.

136
00:08:09,349 --> 00:08:11,533
Owls do not explain everything.

137
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:13,441
Log, the alien file.

138
00:08:13,441 --> 00:08:20,290
The theory: a small craft landed in the gully and its crew, small beings, approached the house.

139
00:08:20,290 --> 00:08:21,300
Let's test it.

140
00:08:21,766 --> 00:08:22,967
First, the craft.

141
00:08:22,967 --> 00:08:29,819
Investigators searched the gully the next day and found no landing marks, no burns, and no metal.

142
00:08:29,819 --> 00:08:30,666
Not a trace.

143
00:08:31,133 --> 00:08:32,596
Second, the military.

144
00:08:32,596 --> 00:08:36,012
Four MPs from Fort Campbell did visit that night.

145
00:08:36,012 --> 00:08:38,939
There are reports the Air Force looked in.

146
00:08:38,939 --> 00:08:41,866
But no official file says what they found.

147
00:08:42,333 --> 00:08:44,230
Third, the cover-up claim.

148
00:08:44,230 --> 00:08:46,931
Some say the case was quietly buried.

149
00:08:46,931 --> 00:08:53,500
But burying a case with dozens of police and reporters as witnesses would be a clumsy job.

150
00:08:53,966 --> 00:08:55,320
Fourth, the beings.

151
00:08:55,320 --> 00:08:57,956
They do not match later alien claims.

152
00:08:57,956 --> 00:09:00,735
They had claws, ears, and glowing skin.

153
00:09:00,735 --> 00:09:05,366
A very different description from the grey aliens of the sixties.

154
00:09:05,833 --> 00:09:13,733
Even the 'spaceship' came from one man, Billy Ray Taylor, and he saw it at dusk, at a distance, before anything else happened.

155
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:18,786
It fits a bright meteor, the kind seen across the region that week.

156
00:09:18,786 --> 00:09:24,399
A fireball with sparks might read as a rainbow-coloured exhaust to a startled eye.

157
00:09:24,866 --> 00:09:28,795
So the alien theory has a landing, no landing site.

158
00:09:28,795 --> 00:09:30,721
It has beings, no bodies.

159
00:09:30,721 --> 00:09:32,878
It has a cover-up, no cover.

160
00:09:32,878 --> 00:09:35,266
It rests entirely on testimony.

161
00:09:35,733 --> 00:09:42,582
But testimony from eleven people, repeated for decades without a profit, is evidence of something.

162
00:09:42,582 --> 00:09:44,399
The question is only what.

163
00:09:44,866 --> 00:09:45,945
Closing the log.

164
00:09:45,945 --> 00:09:47,899
Time to score the Kelly case.

165
00:09:48,366 --> 00:09:55,228
A frightened family, bullet holes, dozens of police and soldiers on the scene: all evidence.

166
00:09:55,228 --> 00:10:00,299
A sincere, unpaid witness group over decades: evidence, and unusual.

167
00:10:00,766 --> 00:10:04,343
An object in the sky, probably a meteor: likely.

168
00:10:04,343 --> 00:10:09,262
Great horned owls explaining the figures: partial, with real gaps.

169
00:10:09,262 --> 00:10:13,733
Little men from space: no landing site, no bodies, no proof.

170
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:16,816
A government cover-up: unverified.

171
00:10:16,816 --> 00:10:18,893
Alien visitation: unproven.

172
00:10:18,893 --> 00:10:24,433
Mass panic and misidentification: the strongest fit, though not perfect.

173
00:10:24,899 --> 00:10:25,729
The verdict.

174
00:10:25,729 --> 00:10:27,112
Probably not aliens.

175
00:10:27,112 --> 00:10:32,780
Most likely a group of frightened people, a meteor, and a pair of very large owls.

176
00:10:32,780 --> 00:10:37,066
But the testimony, and the four-hour night, remain remarkable.

177
00:10:37,533 --> 00:10:43,484
Because whatever was in that yard, eleven people believed they were fighting for their lives.

178
00:10:43,484 --> 00:10:46,299
And that belief never faded for any of them.

179
00:10:46,766 --> 00:10:52,065
Next case: two shipyard workers, a river bank, and creatures with claws for hands.

180
00:10:52,065 --> 00:10:55,166
What happened to them in nineteen seventy-three?

181
00:10:55,633 --> 00:10:56,673
Owls or aliens?

182
00:10:56,673 --> 00:11:02,500
Tell us in the comments, and subscribe for the next ancient mystery put to the test.
